<article class="env-lemma" id="016F">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/016F">Lemma <span data-tag="016F">14.3.6</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a category. Let $U$ be a simplicial object of $\mathcal{C}$. Each of the morphisms $s^ n_ i : U_ n \to U_{n + 1}$ has a left inverse. In particular $s^ n_ i$ is a monomorphism. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is true because $d_ i^{n + 1} \circ s^ n_ i = \text{id}_{U_ n}$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>